<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thihathu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1325</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thihathu (died 1325) was the youngest of three Shan-Burmese brothers who repelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and took power in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> after the fall of Pagan. In 1313 he founded a new capital at Pinya and proclaimed himself heir to the Pagan kings. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saw-yun">Saw Yun</a> broke away to set up a rival court at Sagaing in 1315.</p></div>
